# listend live DB ingest contract

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Invariants

- **File durable when consuming; DB coupled under backpressure.** RabbitMQ ack only after successful archive append. When live ingest is on and DB queues hit the **high watermark** (module constants **0.95** of total byte budget, or any host-affine worker cannot accept another min-floor payload), listend **stops RabbitMQ consume**: nack+requeue **without** archive, `stop_consuming`, wait until usage ≤ **resume watermark 0.50** (and every worker has min-floor headroom) while pumping heartbeats. Overflow stays on the broker ready queue — **not** dropped. `basic_qos(prefetch_count=1)` when live on so pause leaves work on the broker. Watermarks are **module constants** in `listend_db_ingest.py` (not INI). Unexpected `submit` races may still increment `queue_drops` (should stay ~0).
- **`$` rotate hardlinks are unique inodes.** Digit epoch filenames must not share a path with a **different** inode. `_ensure_current_hardlinked_to_timestamp` / new-current `os.link` pick an unused digit name (decrement below cutoff for the pre-unlink safety link; increment from `int(time.time())` for the new `current`). **Never** `os.remove` an epoch path that is a different inode (same-second double `$` would delete the just-closed segment). Any samefile digit name is durable enough to unlink `current`. `_get_first_timestamp_seconds` skips `$` schema host lines (`1 <fqdn>`); only plausible unix seconds (`>= 1e9`) name files. Name collision is recoverable — ack after a unique link, do not nack/requeue. Real I/O (`ENOSPC`, `EACCES`, empty `current` with no timestamp) still fail-closed nack.
- **Never insert incomplete samples.** `host_data` uniqueness / itimes / duplicate-scan use **host + unix-second**. Any row for second `T` without the full event set from that monitor sample makes sync_timedb treat `T` as done → **permanent silent loss** under `ignore_conflicts`. Live path: whole-sample skip without schema (or with schema mismatch / parse failure); no per-type silent drops like the file parser.
- **Host-affine workers** (`hash(host) % N`, stable adler32): per-host `schema_by_host` + `DeltaCarryState`. `$` updates schema; cold-start may seed from on-disk `current` `!` lines. Carry survives `bulk_create` flush; schema/carry not cleared on flush.
- **Batch size** — `listend_db_ingest_batch_samples` (default 100). `$` does not count toward batch. Flush on batch full, idle `queue.get` timeout, or shutdown. Before `proc_data` `bulk_create(..., update_conflicts=True)`, dedupe by `(jid, host, proc)` with **GREATEST** for `vm_peak`/`vm_hwm`/`vm_stk`/`vm_exe`/`vm_lib` and last-write for other KEYS (and raise those peaks from existing DB rows) so multi-sample batches cannot hit Postgres “ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE cannot affect row a second time” and cannot drop job-level memory highs. **host_proc parse:** strip `@fast`/`@full` like host_data; `@fast` uses `schema_fast` (slow keys stay `None`); always `schema_key_basename` on `!host_proc` tokens (`,U=kB`, `,R=S`, …).
- **Queue budget** — `listend_db_ingest_queue_max_gb` (default 8 GiB) total across workers; byte tracker authoritative; Queue `maxsize` derived from budget ÷ min payload floor.
- **Connection recycle** — on idle timeout and max age (`get_db_conn_max_age()` / module constants). No long-lived single connection after one `ensure_django()`.
- **BLAS/OpenMP caps** — spawn workers must call `configure_blas_thread_env()` before importing numpy/pandas (`sync_timedb_parsing`), or 30 workers × default OpenBLAS threads hit `pthread_create` EAGAIN.
- **Strict post-use memory release** — drop message/DataFrame refs after parse; clear ORM batches after flush; reuse `release_spawn_pool_worker_memory` cadence on flush/idle (not every sample). Run **memory-leak review** before close when changing this path.
- **When `listend_db_ingest_enabled`:** sync_timedb must **not** use weak `_try_db_complete_head_tail_fast_path` / `_try_db_complete_tail_window_fast_path`. Fall through to duplicate-timestamp scan (`db_skip=full_scan` when all sample seconds present). Archive/delete gate requires **sync_timedb file-complete mark** (or zero-host mark for proc-only) — never live-only head+tail. Live listend **never** writes the file-complete mark.
- Process titles: `listend.py [main]` / `worker:listend-db-pool`. Extend the existing 10-minute idle monitor with DB counters (`pause_enters`, `db_queued_bytes`).
- **`host_data.jid` from sample header:** digit-line jobid must propagate on stats tags through `compute_deltas_and_arc*` collapse (`"first"` within the group; not a group key) into `host_data.jid`. Idle `-` maps to NULL at ORM (`host_data_instance_from_stats_row`). Same contract for archive `sync_timedb` (shared `sync_timedb_parsing`).

## Canonical modules

| Concern | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Pool / workers / submit / watermarks | `hpcperfstats/dbload/lib/listend_db_ingest.py` |
| Wire + ack + pause/resume consume | `hpcperfstats/listend.py` |
| File-complete mark | `hpcperfstats/dbload/lib/sync_timedb_file_complete_ingest_mark.py` |
| Archive gate | `hpcperfstats/dbload/lib/sync_timedb_ingest_readiness.py` |
| INI | `listend_db_ingest_*` in `[PIPELINE]` via `conf_parser` (queue budget / pool / batch — **not** pause/resume fractions) |

## Residual risk (accepted)

Long DB stalls grow RabbitMQ ready-queue depth (and broker memory/disk). Prefer that over silent live drops. Unexpected race drops of sample *k* can still leave carry reflecting *k−1* while *k+1* is written with a skewed delta (first-writer-wins); sync_timedb repairs missing *seconds* from disk but cannot overwrite live-written keys.

